    "body": "**Judgement calls for the maintainer** (gate green; every shipped machine and golden is byte-identical, so nothing here needs a hand check). Merge order: #477, then #501, then this PR.\n1. **A named machine that states no safe Z is refused by name through this post.** Tormach gets a name exemption in #501; Siemens does not, because no public Siemens document says machine Z0 is the top of travel. The alternative was to keep `G53 Z0` as a convention.\n2. **`millturn.mch` states no `safe_retract`**, so posting it through this post is now refused by name. That's a guess left for the owner.\n3. **`G75` or `SUPA` could replace `G53`.** Both are noted, neither is done, because either would change every Siemens golden.\n4. **The issue text was wrong about tool changes:** the post never lifted Z at a tool change, only after an operation and at program end. No lift was added.",
